        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=Role: IT Support Classifier.\nCategory Context: {{ $('Core Agent').item.json.output.category }}\nBranch Name: {{ $('FInd Branch').item.json.output.branch_name }}\n\nTASK: Classify the user issue into the best Sub-Category from the provided list.\n\nSUB-CATEGORY LIST:\n{{ \n(() => {\n  const inputCat = $('Core Agent').item.json.output.category;\n  const mapCat = { \n    'SW': 'Software', \n    'HW': 'Hardware', \n    'CAMERA': 'Camera', \n    'NETWORK': 'Network', \n    'POS': 'Software',\n    'RATE': 'Software' \n  }[inputCat] || inputCat; \n\n  return $('Get Sub Category').all()\n    .filter(item => item.json.sub_category === mapCat || item.json.sub_category === inputCat)\n    .map(item => {\n        const aliasInfo = item.json.alias ? ` [Keywords: ${item.json.alias}]` : '';\n        return `- ${item.json.name}${aliasInfo}`;\n    })\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n})() \n}}\n\nRULES:\n1. PRINTER PRIORITY: If query mentions \"Printer/Paper\", select \"Printer\" immediately.\n2. BRANCH MAPPING: For NETWORK category, prioritize \"Internet PPontime\" only if the \"Branch Name\" has a 100% exact match in its keywords. If multiple ISPs contain the same branch name, cross-check with the issue intensity or use a pre-defined mapping table.\n3. IMPACT: Prioritize work-blocking issues (Login/Transaction) over cosmetic ones.\n4. FALLBACK RULE: If the issue does not fit any sub-category from the provided list, or if the list is empty, you must return the value of the \"Category Context\" as the sub_category.\n\nReturn ONLY the Sub-Category name."
            }
          ]
        },
